DATASET CITATIONS AND EMPIRICAL RESEARCH ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS
===============================================================================

PredictIQ incorporates data structures, benchmarks, and statistical models
evaluated against empirical software engineering research datasets. We gratefully
acknowledge the original researchers and curators of these benchmark datasets:

1. China Dataset (499 projects)
   Origin: PROMISE Software Engineering Repository.
   Citations:
   - Menzies, T., Krishna, R., & Pryor, D. (2015). The Promise Repository of
     Empirical Software Engineering Data. West Virginia University.
   - Public domain empirical software effort data from Chinese software enterprises.

2. Kitchenham Dataset (145 projects)
   Origin: Commercial banking and retail applications.
   Citations:
   - Kitchenham, B. A., & Känsälä, K. (1993). Inter-item consistency in software
     metrics data: An empirical study. Information and Software Technology.
   - Kitchenham, B. A., Pfleeger, S. L., McColl, B., & Eagan, S. (2002).
     Preliminary guidelines for empirical research in software engineering.
     IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering, 28(8), 721-734.

3. Desharnais Dataset (81 projects)
   Origin: Canadian business software applications.
   Citations:
   - Desharnais, J. M. (1989). Analyse statistique de la productivité des projets
     informatique à partie de la technique des points de fonction. Master's Thesis,
     Université du Québec à Montréal.
   - PROMISE Software Engineering Repository.

4. Maxwell Dataset (62 projects)
   Origin: European Space Agency / aerospace software applications.
   Citations:
   - Maxwell, K. D. (2002). Applied Statistics for Software Managers.
     Prentice Hall PTR.

5. Albrecht Dataset (24 projects)
   Origin: IBM corporate data processing applications.
   Citations:
   - Albrecht, A. J., & Gaffney, J. E. (1983). Software function, source lines
     of code, and development effort prediction: A software science validation.
     IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering, SE-9(6), 639-648.

6. AT&T Aptness Dataset (104 projects)
   Origin: Telecommunications systems.
   Citations:
   - Matson, J. E., Barrett, B. E., & Mellichamp, J. M. (1994). Software
     development cost estimation using function points. IEEE Transactions on
     Software Engineering, 20(4), 275-287.

7. Finnish Dataset (38 projects - Reference / Benchmark)
   Citations:
   - Kitchenham, B., & Känsälä, K. (1993). Inter-item consistency in software
     metrics data. Empirical Software Engineering.

8. Huijgens Enterprise Dataset (492 projects - Reference / Benchmark)
   Citations:
   - Huijgens, H., van Deursen, A., & Minkman, R. (2020). Huijgens 492
     Enterprise Software Project Dataset. Empirical Software Engineering.
